VALUES (
  '2026/10/16/hdq-thread-oct-16-2026',
  'thread', 'thread',
  'Oil Rose 10% This Week and the Canadian Dollar Gained 0.8%: Crude Is No Longer Carrying the Loonie', 'WTI settled at $101.41, about the September 16 price, yet the Canadian dollar is 1.5% weaker and the 10-year yield 9 basis points lower, and three calm readings from this morning ended together.',
  '<ul>
<li><strong>WTI settled at $101.41 on Friday, up 10.4% on the week,</strong><span> while the Canadian dollar gained only 0.8% to about 70.7 US cents.</span></li>
<li><strong>Oil is back near its September 16 level and the dollar is not.</strong><span> USD/CAD moved from 1.3947 to 1.4154 and the 10-year yield fell from 3.92% to 3.83% as of October 15.</span></li>
<li><strong>The largest recent yield drop came on jobs day, not oil day.</strong><span> The 10-year fell 7 basis points to 3.86% on October 9 as 68,000 jobs were lost.</span></li>
<li><strong>Three morning calms ended together.</strong><span> WTI crossed $100, the VIX rose above 20 from 16.46, and the TSX noon print of 36,338.36 sat above its 22-session band.</span></li>
<li><strong>September CPI on Monday decides which channel wins.</strong><span> The Bank of Canada decides on October 28 with its policy rate at 2.25% against a Fed range of 3.75% to 4.00%.</span></li>
</ul>',
  '<h2>Oil Rose Twelve Times as Fast as the Currency</h2>
<p>West Texas Intermediate settled at $101.41 on Friday, up 3.5% on the day and 10.4% on the week, after Brent closed at $109.86 following its first touch of $110 since May. The Canadian dollar traded near 70.70 US cents at midday, up about 0.3% on the day and 0.8% on the week. Oil moved about twelve times as far as the currency, and the Geopolitical desk argued this morning that the market was pricing duration rather than a spike. Friday priced it, and the loonie did not follow.</p>
<p>WTI round-tripped from $102.43 on September 16 to an $88.28 low on October 7 and back to $101.41, while USD/CAD climbed in one direction from 1.3947 to a high of 1.4271 on October 9 and has only partly reversed. The oil price completed a loop and the currency did not.</p>
